        "original_id": "d36b710a-9614-577c-992a-e5f48aa63396",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Dill, Jean-Philippe Rameau, Voltaire, Giacomo Puccini\n- Works: Castor et Pollux, Samson, Manon Lescaut\n- Topics: Opera composition, aesthetics\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Dill proposes that Jean-Philippe Rameau composed Castor et Pollux in 1737 just after working with Voltaire on the unfinished opera Samson.\n- Charles Dill proposes that after Samson was left incomplete, Jean-Philippe Rameau composed Castor et Pollux using Voltaire's aesthetics.\n- Giacomo Puccini composed the four-act opera Manon Lescaut between 1890 and 1893.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
